Jackal
======

Jackal is a compiler for a small custom language (`.jkl` files), written in C.
It lexes (flex) -> parses (bison) -> builds an AST -> compiles to a linear,
stack-based IR bytecode intended for a separate VM, *jackalvm*. The VM is not in
this repo; this is the compiler plus its support library, libjackal.

Pipeline:

    source.jkl -> lexer -> parser -> AST -> jkl_compile() -> jkl_ir_t[] -> .bin

Status: a working but incomplete prototype. The front end and the back end for
literals, arithmetic (with precedence), variables (resolved to symbol-table
slots), control flow (if/else/loop), and call/func/return are implemented and
tested; the class system, optimizer, and evaluator are scaffolding. See
docs/roadmap.md for the honest feature matrix.

Build
-----

Prereqs: a C toolchain plus `autoconf automake bison flex pkg-config`. The
`Check` unit-test library is optional (the test harness falls back to a
dependency-free shim when it is absent).

    ./autogen.sh        # bootstrap autotools (runs autoreconf -i)
    ./configure
    make                # builds libjackal.a and the `jackal` binary

Run
---

    ./jackal samples/main.jkl          # writes main.bin (versioned "JKLB" bytecode)
    ./jackal samples/main.jkl out.bin  # explicit output path

Test
----

    make check          # runs the unit + integration test suites

The tests can also be run directly without autotools:

    cd tests && make compiler          # unit tests
    cd tests && make precedence        # integration tests (built under ASan)

Documentation
-------------

Start with docs/README.md (index) and CLAUDE.md (orientation for working in this
repo). Deeper references: architecture.md, language.md, ir.md, modules.md,
